cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExomeFlow in your research, please cite it using this metadata."
title: "ExomeFlow: A Production-Quality Python Package for Automated Whole Exome Sequencing Analysis"
version: 2.2.13
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20155767
date-released: "2026-05-13"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Robin
    email: itsrobintomar@gmail.com
    affiliation: "All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS), New Delhi, India"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-9084-2019"
abstract: >
  ExomeFlow is a Python package that provides a complete, automated Whole Exome
  Sequencing (WES) analysis workflow from raw FASTQ files to functionally annotated
  variants in a single reproducible CLI command. It implements GATK best-practice
  variant calling (fastp → BWA MEM → BQSR → HaplotypeCaller → hard filtering) with
  ANNOVAR functional annotation against 8 databases (refGene, ClinVar, gnomAD,
  dbNSFP, COSMIC, ExAC, avSNP150, dbscSNV). Features include multi-sample cohort
  processing, checkpointing, structured logging, and Docker/Singularity support.
keywords:
